    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i have a 2018 honda civic and every time i hit the gas there is this really loud squealing noise coming from under the hood. can u explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why a bad one would make that sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt in your 2018 Honda Civic helps drive essential components like the alternator, power steering pump, and air conditioning compressor by turning them via a single long belt. A bad belt makes a loud squealing noise because it has become stretched or worn, failing to grip the pulleys properly and slipping under the load of the engine. To fix this, you should have a mechanic inspect the belt and tensioner immediately to prevent overheating the alternator or damaging the power steering system.",
