    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the info. so if it is slipping, is it just because the belt is old or could something else be causing it? like could the tensioner be the problem or is it usually just the belt itself?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While an aging belt is a very common culprit, the noisy squealing frequently stems from a failing tensioner that no longer maintains proper belt pressure. If the pulley bearings inside the tensioner are worn, they create play that allows the belt to slacken and slip when you hit the gas. It is difficult to diagnose the exact source at home without tools, but an inspection often reveals whether the issue lies with the belt itself or the supporting tensioner assembly.",
      "source": "target",
